data
  title timeout vs shield: two orthogonal axes
  desc One bounds how long; the other bounds who may interrupt — you need both
  compares
    - label asyncio.timeout
      children
        - label asyncio.timeout — bounds DURATION
        - label call_at timer cancels its own body at expiry
        - label CancelledError becomes TimeoutError at the boundary
        - label uncancel() count lets nested scopes compose
        - label Limits WHEN work ends, not who interrupts
    - label asyncio.shield
      children
        - label asyncio.shield — bounds INTERRUPTION
        - label Outer cancel hits the waiter, not the inner task
        - label Inner work keeps running detached
        - label No kept reference orphans its result and errors
        - label Limits WHO may interrupt, not how long
